## Context
Found by the verify-gate of PR #1743 (ticket 1247, 2026-10-27). 1247 replaced the helper paragraph
with a one-line fallback (preset `IDH_ROOT` wins; a skill directory or a SKILL.md path resolve the
same root). Four sites outside that paragraph still derive the root unconditionally from
`dirname(<loaded-SKILL.md>)/../..`: `skills/roar/SKILL.md:27`, `skills/roar/runbooks/sweep.md:23`,
`skills/roar/runbooks/capture.md:92`, `skills/trace-doctor/SKILL.md:38` (`HARNESS_DIR`). Under Claude
Code, which supplies the skill directory, each resolves one level too high, and the roar lines
overwrite the `IDH_ROOT` that `shell-init.sh` now exports, so roar's attribution helpers can run
from the wrong place. `skills/roar/close-and-clean.sh:60` already keeps a preset value.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The four sites use 1247's canonical fallback line (or read the preset `IDH_ROOT`), so a preset
      wins and a directory or a SKILL.md path resolve the same root.
- [ ] `tests/test_skill_seam.py` (or a sibling) fails on an unconditional `dirname(<loaded-SKILL.md>)`
      derivation anywhere under `skills/`.
- [ ] The harness gate passes.

## Relevant files
skills/roar/SKILL.md, skills/roar/runbooks/sweep.md, skills/roar/runbooks/capture.md,
skills/trace-doctor/SKILL.md, tests/test_skill_seam.py

Related: [[1247]], [[1240]].
